      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Glad you posted this TummyTime as I too was having this problem but thankfully I found the cause with some other friends. I'm guessing after the recent update the banner got put on the same layer as the nameplate (not sure if intentional as when VRC updates random things do like to break lol) When Opacity is set at 0% it also causes the banner to disappear. As seen in my images, the first image is with opacity at 100% and the second is at 0% I like the cleaner look of the nameplates at 0% as well (preferably without the banners vanishing) I'm sure they can fix this issue with the banner layer relatively quickly.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
